From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Adam Matthews <52178922+adamsthws@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 15:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] emulator: keep the slow tick on the device clock

The slow tick restarted its count from the chunk it was raised in, so what
that chunk overshot its period by was lost. A chunk steps insn_count by 1000
in one state, but by 420 (ARM to Thumb) or 2381 (Thumb to ARM) where it
crosses between them, as one taking or leaving an interrupt does: on a
BK7238 OpenBeken or ESPHome image the tick came every 10,500 of insn_count,
not 10,000, and every 10,900 under a BL0937's 1.8 kHz of pulses. The guest's
RTOS tick, raised here, ran 5-9% slow against insn_count, the clock the rest
of the device keeps, and a meter counting pulses over a second of the
guest's time read that much high.

Each tick is now due SLOW_TICK_INSNS after the last was due. A step is
always shorter than a period, so one is raised each period; the idle skip
already aims at last_slow + SLOW_TICK_INSNS. tests/slow_tick.py fails
without it: 1333 ticks for 1444 periods.

Firmware now gets about 5% fewer instructions per millisecond of its own
time, so nine self-tests' expectations that hang on timing alone are
re-recorded:

- CC8000 A19 and A60 2.0.4.51 print tick=179 where they printed 172, and
  A60 2.0.3.47 tick=180 where 173; their GPIO checks failed only because
  the run stopped at the missing line.
- Zengge ZJ21413 and XGD-NZ-002 print their BRMT task's start at 2470 and
  2664 ms, not 2408 and 2588.
- BIM8774 reports 67424 bytes free at device_init, not 67376.
- The SDK banner of the Tuya device in factory mode, TH01's
  Wakeup_GetEvent line and the CB3S IR module's app version and
  BLE_STACK_OK lines come out cut by other tasks' lines; each now looks
  for a line printed intact beside them that says the same.
